            <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs leading-relaxed">
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Metal Bonded Cup Tools</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Super-hard metal bond with no elasticity and excellent heat resistance for heavy stock removal on straight-line and CNC edgers (profiles 6A2/11A2/9A3). GreatDia-style segmented or continuous rims hold form at high feed; KAYES Chennai high-temp sintering and CNC balancing delivers micron concentricity and long high-speed life with low chipping.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Resin Bonded Cup Tools</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Elastic resin bond, self-sharpening and non-clogging for fine arrissing and finish after metal cups. Ideal for tempered and low-E glass where light touch prevents micro-chips. KAYES fully-automatic mixing and curing in Chennai — using UK/German-sourced diamonds — ensures consistent density, mirror-like finish and durability run after run.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Grinding Wheels</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Peripheral and cup grinding wheels (1A1, 3A1, 14A1, 1A1R, D150) for stock removal, shaping and slitting across solar, appliance and automotive glass. GreatDia highlights high grinding efficiency — diamond metal cut exceeds other abrasives on hard-brittle materials; KAYES adds CNC-balanced bodies and strict QC for vibration-free, high-speed durability and exact size holding.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Drills</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Sintered thin-wall core drills and integrated drill-ream bits (OD 4–150 mm, G½ Belgian shank, internal coolant) for clean, chip-free holes in architectural, automotive and lab glass. Force-balanced design gives strong guidance with minimal radial vibration, plus dynamic flow channels for fast chip evacuation and low friction; KAYES Chennai holds micron tolerances on wall 0.8–1.2 mm for consistent breakout-free drilling.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Milling Tools / Routers</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Diamond finger and router bits with slotted sintered tips for notches, cut-outs and internal shaping on Bavelloni/Bottero CNC centres. Different patented diamond layouts give strong attack and wear resistance while optimised hydraulics clear chips. KAYES supplies M14/M22 and ½ Gas variants, CNC-balanced in Chennai for high-speed stability and long life on every pass.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Seamer</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Light peripheral seaming wheels for quick de-burring of cut edges before tempering and handling. Removes the razor edge without taking full edge — fast, low-chipping, perfect for high-volume lines. KAYES seaming wheels are high-efficiency resin/metal hybrids, Chennai-made to run cool and hold dimension at line speed.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Counter Sunk Tools</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Countersink/cone drills that drill and chamfer in one stroke for shower, furniture and structural glass. Integrated 60°+ cone gives uniform countersink depth with low friction and long life. KAYES holds the included angle and diameter to microns in Chennai, so fittings seat flush with no secondary grinding.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Pencil Edge Wheels</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Profile pencil-rounding wheels (single and double-groove, R2–R3.5, D150 class) that form the classic soft “pencil” radius on auto and architectural glass. Metal-bond diamond shapes the edge while maintaining brilliant geometry; KAYES high-temp bond and balanced steel bodies ensure the radius repeats to micron tolerance at high-speed feed.</p></div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50"><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Arrising Wheels</h4><p class="mt-1 text-slate-600">Fine resin arris wheels that put the tiny 45° chamfer on top/bottom edges after cutting — the final safety against edge chips in tempering and handling. Self-sharpening resin, fine grits (#180–#600+) prevent cracks spreading from the cut line. KAYES Chennai-moulded resin, polished on fully automatic lines, delivers consistent chamfer width and high-speed durability on low-E and clear glass alike.</p></div>
